---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../data/site';

const title = 'Crit vs Vulnerable in Diablo 4 – Which Bucket to Feed';
const description =
  'Crit versus Vulnerable in Diablo IV: how the two buckets differ, how uptime changes the math, and how to decide which affix your build should chase next.';
const updated = SITE.lastVerified;
---

<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Guides' }, { name: 'Crit vs Vulnerable' }]}
  schema={[{
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Article',
    headline: 'Crit vs Vulnerable in Diablo IV',
    datePublished: '2026-10-08',
    dateModified: updated,
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE.brand },
  }]}
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>Crit vs Vulnerable</h1>
    <div class="h1-bar"></div>
    <p class="lede">
      The two best damage buckets in the game, and the eternal reroll question between them. The answer is
      arithmetic — small bucket beats big bucket — with one twist: uptime.
    </p>
    <div class="microline"><span>By {SITE.brand}</span><span>Updated {updated}</span></div>
  </div>

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Quick answer</h2>
    <p>
      Crit multipliers apply only when you crit (so crit <em>chance</em> gates the bucket); vulnerable applies
      whenever the enemy is vulnerable (so <em>uptime</em> gates it). Whichever condition you satisfy more
      reliably is the bucket worth feeding first — check both gates in the <a href="/damage-calculator/">damage calculator</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>The twist: uptime beats size</h2>
    <pre class="formula">vuln bucket ×1.8 at 40% uptime → avg gain 1 + 0.4×0.8 = ×1.32
crit  bucket ×2.0 at 60% chance → avg gain 1 + 0.6×1.0 = ×1.60</pre>
    <p>
      A bigger multiplier with worse availability loses. This is why "always take vulnerable" and "always take
      crit" are both wrong — the answer is conditional on your build's uptime and crit chance, which is why
      the comparator works from <em>your</em> numbers: <a href="/stat-priority/">stat priority comparator</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Rules of thumb that hold up</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Below ~40% crit chance:</strong> crit damage affixes underperform — fix the chance first.</li>
      <li><strong>Below ~50% vulnerable uptime:</strong> vulnerable affixes underperform — fix the uptime (aspects, skills) first.</li>
      <li><strong>Both gates satisfied:</strong> feed whichever bucket is currently smaller; rerun the comparator after each big change.</li>
      <li><strong>Additive last:</strong> it shares one bucket with everything else — the classic trap explained in <a href="/guides/how-damage-works/">how damage works</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The 30-second decision</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>Enter current stats in the <a href="/stat-priority/">comparator</a>.</li>
      <li>Set option A to the additive affix, option B to the crit/vulnerable affix you're considering.</li>
      <li>Take the bigger marginal gain. If within ~1% of each other, take the one matching your playstyle variance (crit for burst, vuln for sustained).</li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</Base>
